# ColorTreeField

## Summary

A Munsell color pick as a field. Reach for it when a flat color picker is not enough: the **edit format is the full 3D studio** (`ColorTreeStudio`) bounded to the form, so a card author gets perceptual hue/value/chroma picking on any card with one `contains()`. The value is the picked `hex` (a `ColorField`) plus its Munsell `munsell` notation (a `StringField`). The embedded format is a compact swatch + hex + notation strip; the atom format is a tiny swatch + notation.

## Import

```javascript
import { ColorTreeField } from '../color-tree-field';
```

## Usage

```gts
export class MyCard extends CardDef {
  @field accentColor = contains(ColorTreeField);
}
```

Rendering:

```hbs
<@fields.accentColor @format='edit' />   {{! the 3D studio picker }}
<@fields.accentColor />                  {{! swatch + hex + notation }}
<@fields.accentColor @format='atom' />   {{! tiny swatch + notation }}
```

Picking happens in the studio's atlas view: open the atlas, hold a spot on the page, and the field's `hex`/`munsell` are set (and the hex copied to the clipboard).
